# HERO SECTION — QuantFun Web

## Objective

Implement the Hero section exactly as shown in the approved homepage design.

This document replaces every previous Hero implementation.

The uploaded homepage mockup is the primary and authoritative design reference.

Do not redesign.

Do not reinterpret.

Do not modernize.

The objective is visual fidelity.

The Hero should immediately communicate:

- Institutional
- Editorial
- Contemporary Museum
- Luxury Annual Report
- Architectural Minimalism

Everything should feel quiet, spacious, and intentional.

---

# Existing Components

The Navbar has already been completed.

Do NOT modify it.

Simply render the Hero beneath the existing Navbar.

---

# Section Structure

```jsx
<main>
  <Navbar />
  <Hero />
  ...sections
</main>
```

The Hero is responsible only for the landing composition.

---

# Hero Height

Desktop only.

Height: 100vh

Minimum height: 900px

The Hero should completely fill the first viewport.

No scrolling should occur before the Hero finishes.

---

# Layout

The Hero consists of two visual layers.

Layer 1: Background illustration

Layer 2: Typography

The illustration sits behind the content.

The typography always stays readable.

---

# Background Illustration

Image source: public/img/bg-hero.png

The image fills the right 2/3 of the viewport (w-2/3).

Alignment: Right center, object-right-top.

The image should naturally overflow beyond the viewport on the right.

Do not contain the image fully.

Do not center it.

No rotation.

No blur.

No floating animation.

No parallax.

No shadow effects (on the image).

The illustration itself is already the visual statement.

---

# Hero Content

Content is left aligned.

Everything begins at the 260px left padding (aligned with navbar).

The content block sits in the left portion of the viewport.

Large whitespace on the right is intentional (occupied by the bg image).

Do not attempt to visually center the content.

---

# Main Heading

Text:

BUILDING CLARITY,
IN COMPLEXITY.

Typography:

Font: Cormorant Garamond

Weight: 300 (Light)

Style: Uppercase

Font Size: 64px

Letter spacing: 0.16em

Line Height: 1.05

Color: #111111

Drop shadow: 0_-2px_4px rgba(0,0,0,0.12)

The heading should become the strongest visual element on the page.

---

# Supporting Keywords

Immediately below the heading.

Text: Data • Logic • Insight

Font: Cormorant Garamond

Weight: 300 (Light)

Font Size: 24px

Color: #222222

Opacity: 70%

Bullets: black square boxes (8x8px), vertically centered.

Spacing between words: generous (gap-16).

Keep them calm and understated.

---

# Content Position

The content block sits in the upper-middle portion of the Hero.

Navbar (72px) → content is vertically centered via flex.

Main Heading

↓ 40px

Supporting Keywords

Maintain generous whitespace around every element.

Avoid vertical compression.

---

# Animation

Very subtle. Only once on initial page load.

Heading: Opacity 0→1, TranslateY 12px→0. Duration: 2s. Ease: easeIn.

Keywords: Opacity 0→1 (no Y movement). Duration: 2s. Ease: easeIn. Delay: 3s (1s after heading finishes).

Elements stay visible after animation completes (no loop).

Background illustration: Static. No movement.

---

# Component Architecture

components/sections/Hero.tsx

The Hero component should only render presentation.

Do not place navigation logic here.

Keep responsibilities separated.

---

# Technical Requirements

Framework: Next.js (App Router)

Language: TypeScript

Styling: Tailwind CSS

Animation: Framer Motion (minimal usage)

No inline styles.

No hardcoded positioning hacks.

Keep spacing reusable where practical.

---

# Visual Fidelity Rules

The approved homepage mockup is the highest priority.

Implementation order:
1. Match composition
2. Match spacing
3. Match typography
4. Match illustration scale
5. Match alignment
6. Match visual rhythm

Do not add extra decorations.
Do not invent gradients.
Do not add glassmorphism.
Do not add cards.
Do not add colored accents.
Do not introduce unnecessary animations.

Every pixel should move closer to the reference image, never further away.

